{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Logrotate parsed the file as a one-day policy, and the persistent daily systemd timer was enabled, active, and scheduled before and after reboot. A scoped forced rotation also completed successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f54a5f7d63a4bc8","cmd-912b1f0ce1c34b1e","cmd-69dafef386f54089","cmd-bca3c537dbd949ef"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective policy reports seven rotations with compression. Rotation produced a valid gzip archive containing the prior records, and the policy and archive persisted across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-69dafef386f54089","cmd-1c786cb307394ed1","cmd-dd9937d6f94c4e56","cmd-bca3c537dbd949ef"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow writing to continue after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A writer opened the log before rotation; copytruncate preserved inode 80283 and the open descriptor during rotation. The same writer then wrote the post-rotation record to the current log, while its pre-rotation record appeared in the compressed archive.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb507bcfcfbd42ba","cmd-69dafef386f54089","cmd-1c786cb307394ed1"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. State changes were causally justified: installing logrotate, creating the policy, enabling its timer, running a bounded writer/rotation probe, removing its temporary files, and performing the mandatory restart. The two retained test records and generated archive were bounded behavioral evidence. After execution there were no failed services, package consistency remained healthy, temporary probe files were absent, and socket differences were only reboot-related PID churn. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart timer, policy, archive, and data state; acknowledged restart; changed boot identity; and recovered system, timer, policy, package, archive, and data state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-087a2745e9e149f2","cmd-b7c5620a6f474590","cmd-912b1f0ce1c34b1e","cmd-eb507bcfcfbd42ba","cmd-69dafef386f54089","cmd-1c786cb307394ed1","cmd-dd9937d6f94c4e56","cmd-1cd5a08fc7754cf7","cmd-bca3c537dbd949ef","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied, and node1 also completed the provider-wide restart protocol with coherent recovery evidence and an independently confirmed boot-identity change.","limitations":["The evidence did not observe an unforced rotation after a full day or exercise eight successive rotations; daily cadence and seven-archive retention are established through the active scheduler, parsed effective policy, and one successful compressed rotation.","The continuity probe used a controlled open-descriptor writer because discovery showed no running inventory application writer; it directly validates the configured file-writing behavior but is not an observation of a real application process."]}
